ists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yankscally/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T21:59:32Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T22:00:57Z","body":"For game development, a feature like this is extremely powerful because you can use the gltf as a \"3D .zip file\".\r\n\r\nThat data could be a bunch of different meshes from an asset pack, so that you are able to extract the resources you need without making a scene. \r\n\r\nUsing scenes to export a bunch of components like this I find strange, but this PR unlocks a lot of potential by allowing developers to package assets much more efficiently for game development purposes. It changes the precedent for how gltf could be used, and I think this is very worthwhile","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353931442/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3399535390","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107836#issuecomment-3399535390","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107836","id":3399535390,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KoMse","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"